message.content:
Phase 0 for DASH-247: execute your Phase 0 deliverables (sections 1–4 of your agent definition) in this worktree.

Spec: `CLAUDE.md`, `PLAN.md` §5–§6 **as superseded by PLAN §13 (2026-09-28 entry)** — §13 wins wherever it differs (§5.1 index, §5.2 API contract, §5.3 rules, §5.4 copy, §7 goldens). `docs/design-consensus.md` holds the rationale; its architect handoff "Next" line lists contract requirements you must include:
- `BaselineAssessment` with `WeeksUsed` plus nullable `Median`, `Low`, `High`, `Deviation` (status always present);
- `NormalityOptions { BaselineWeeks = 8, MinimumEligibleWeeks = 4, BandWidth = 2.0, SpreadFloor = 1.0 }`;
- non-null `EarliestWeek` (= `LatestCompleteWeek` when the account has no events) and `MinimumEligibleWeeks` in the report and the API DTO;
- the sites query is unbounded (no `beforeUtc`); the anchor query returns only the global `MAX(occurred_at)`;
- `IAccountService` exists (endpoints call services only, never queries).
API DTOs and TS models must match the §13 §5.2 JSON exactly (including `minimumEligibleWeeks`, always-present `baseline` object).

Rules: structure and contracts only — `NotImplementedException` stubs, no logic, no SQL, no tests. `git mv schema.sql seed.sql db/` content untouched. No comment blocks.

When done: `dotnet build` (0 warnings), `cd web && npm run build` and `npm test` must succeed — paste trimmed output. Commit all your work on this worktree's branch (message ends with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`). Do not touch the main worktree.
Report with the CLAUDE.md handoff format, the full public contract listing, **and the worktree path and branch name**. List anything in the spec you found ambiguous under "Uncertain" rather than guessing silently.
